From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO Manga Continue Reading

Add "Continue reading" to manga mode. While the reader is open, the
browser asks the page script every 2 seconds where the user is (the
image at the top of the screen and how far into it) and keeps, for each
series, the last chapter read, the place in it and a cover. The series
and chapter number come from the page title (og:title, the title or the
heading, like "Series - Chapter 12 | Site") or from the address (like
/manga/series/chapter-12/); the cover is the series cover of the page
(og:image) or the first page of the chapter, downloaded through the
page so that sites that check the referrer still send it.

The new tab page gets a "Continue reading" row with the covers of the
last 12 series, a progress bar and the chapter. A tap opens the chapter
and the reader scrolls back to the same place, keeping it while the
images above load; a chapter read to the end opens the next one. A long
press removes a series. Opening a chapter that the user read part of in
any other way also goes back to the place.

While the user reads, the next chapter and its first 10 images load in
the background once 60% of the chapter is read, so that it opens
faster. A check box in the manga mode dialog turns this off.

Nothing is kept for incognito tabs, and the Fire button forgets the
series along with the history.

